image_loading=&#8221;default&#8221; id=&#8221;1781316155641-8&#8243; title=&#8221;Item&#8221; tab_id=&#8221;1781316155642-7&#8243;][team_member image_url=&#8221;386&#8243; bio_image_url=&#8221;386&#8243; team_memeber_style=&#8221;bio_fullscreen&#8221; image_loading=&#8221;default&#8221; team_member_bio_full_html=&#8221;simple&#8221; name=&#8221;Ustadh Abdurrahman Wood&#8221; job_position=&#8221;Instructor&#8221; team_member_bio=&#8221;Ustadh Abdurrahman Justin Wood is an American Imam, Speaker, and Leader born and raised in Columbus, Ohio. He accepted Islam at age 17 after studying the life of Malcolm X and researching religion and philosophy. To gain a deeper understanding of Arabic and Islamic sciences, he traveled to Makkah, Saudi Arabia and completed an American Imam certificate course. Upon returning to the United States, he focused on helping young American Muslims embrace the relevance and practicality of Islam, establishing and supporting youth initiatives in multiple communities. He also serves as Ameer of AlMaghrib&#8217;s Columbus, Ohio.&#8221; social_icon_1=&#8221;fa fa-instagram&#8221; social_link_1=&#8221;https:\/\/www.instagram.com\/abdurrahmanjustinwood\/&#8221;][\/team_member][\/item][item simple_slider_bg_image_position=&#8221;default&#8221; simple_slider_overlay_strength=&#8221;0.3&#8243; simple_slider_bg_image_loading=&#8221;default&#8221; id=&#8221;1781316155744-2&#8243; title=&#8221;Item&#8221; tab_id=&#8221;1781316155746-8&#8243;][team_member image_url=&#8221;522&#8243; bio_image_url=&#8221;522&#8243; team_memeber_style=&#8221;bio_fullscreen&#8221; image_loading=&#8221;default&#8221; team_member_bio_full_html=&#8221;simple&#8221; name=&#8221;Ustadh Mohamed Noor&#8221; job_position=&#8221;Instructor&#8221; team_member_bio=&#8221;Ustadh Mohamed Noor is a dedicated instructor at Siraaj Institute and Ma&#8217;had ibn Taymiyah. Involved in Dawah since age 15, he has more than a decade of experience in Islamic education and outreach. For almost a decade, he has taught Arabic grammar, Hadith, Tafseer, Aqeedah, and Fiqh. Ustadh Mohamed began his studies in Columbus, Ohio, graduating from the Ma&#8217;had at Masjid ibn Taymiyyah, and has studied with scholars from Somalia, Egypt, Saudi Arabia, Nigeria, and Senegal. He also pursued advanced studies abroad in Egypt and Saudi Arabia. His diverse educational background, along with his commitment to nurturing the next generation of Muslim scholars and leaders, make him a highly respected figure within the community.&#8221; social_icon_1=&#8221;fa fa-instagram&#8221; social_link_1=&#8221;https:\/\/www.instagram.com\/mohamedcnoor\/&#8221;][\/team_member][\/item][item simple_slider_bg_image_position=&#8221;default&#8221; simple_slider_overlay_strength=&#8221;0.3&#8243; simple_slider_bg_image_loading=&#8221;default&#8221; id=&#8221;1781316155834-6&#8243; title=&#8221;Item&#8221; tab_id=&#8221;1781316155835-5&#8243;][team_member image_url=&#8221;521&#8243; bio_image_url=&#8221;521&#8243; team_memeber_style=&#8221;bio_fullscreen&#8221; image_loading=&#8221;default&#8221; team_member_bio_full_html=&#8221;simple&#8221; name=&#8221;Sheikh Hassan Noor&#8221; job_position=&#8221;Instructor&#8221; team_member_bio=&#8221;Sheikh Hassan Noor is an accomplished scholar specializing in Islamic law. He graduated with First Class honors from the College of Islamic Law at Imam University in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, and is currently pursuing a Master\u2019s Degree in legal theory at Al-Madinah International University in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia.<\/p>\n<p>With years of teaching experience at Ibnu Taymiyah Islamic Center in Columbus, Sheikh Hassan is known for his insightful presentations on Islamic jurisprudence. He has taught courses in Arabic, Fiqh, Legal Theory, and Islamic Texts.&#8221; social_icon_1=&#8221;fa fa-instagram&#8221; social_link_1=&#8221;https:\/\/www.instagram.com\/hassannoor.oh\/&#8221;][\/team_member][\/item][\/carousel][\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row type=&#8221;full_width_